STAGED PATCH 0004 of 5: apply after 0005.
Targets: Linux 6.12.116, mm/percpu.c and lib/genalloc.c.
Line anchors are the patch-point list's numbers of record;
context lines are schematic. Re-base on the real tree
before applying.

Subject: iscandar: the second ring (4.2, 4.3); 4.1 by backing

Center 4.1 (mempool) takes no hunk: a mempool over slab is
redirected at 1.1 with its elements, and a mempool over
pages draws on the substrate, exactly as the
reconciliation disposes the family. The bridge protocol
carries an op for it (OP_MEMPOOL_ALLOC) for pools whose
element door the build wires directly; the layer answers
the pages backing with BRIDGE_SUBSTRATE, named, not served.

Center 4.2 (percpu): the redirect stands at the center, as
ruled. Stated plainly, as the reconciliation states it:
the chunk layer carves internally beneath this center, and
redirecting the center is a separate design question from
the boot-load families. The staged hunk redirects the
center's backing: one bridge run serves the whole per-cpu
area (size times the possible CPU count), and the chunk
bookkeeping stays the kernel's over that run. Whether the
chunk layer's internal carving is compatible with that
shape is build-time design work this staging does not
settle; it is carried as an open item in BUILD-STATUS.md.
The center's earliest traffic (its first chunks) falls in
the early-boot prefix and is stock and logged there, not
missed.

Center 4.3 (gen_pool): genalloc manages device and special
memory pools, not general system RAM. The redirect is
gated: only a pool the build has registered as an arena
pool (0005) is served at the bridge; every other pool is
stock, by the boundary the patch list records. The
reconciliation follows ruling 5 for the center and records
the served set as open; the registration gate is where the
build names the set, one pool at a time, each naming a
decision of record. For a registered pool, the pool's
managed range IS the arena's kernel mapping, so the
address the center returns is the arena base plus the
bridge offset.

--- a/mm/percpu.c
+++ b/mm/percpu.c
@@ -1743,7 +1743,26 @@
-void __percpu *pcpu_alloc_noprof(size_t size, size_t align, bool reserved, ...)
+void __percpu *pcpu_alloc_noprof(size_t size, size_t align, bool reserved, ...)
 {
+	if (iscandar_active() && !reserved) {
+		struct IscandarBridgeRecord rec = { };
+
+		rec.op = ISCANDAR_OP_PERCPU_ALLOC;
+		rec.size = (u64)size * num_possible_cpus();
+		rec.align = (u32)align;
+		if (iscandar_bridge_call(&rec)
+		    || rec.status != ISCANDAR_BRIDGE_OK)
+			return NULL;
+		return (void __percpu *)
+			iscandar_offset_to_ptr(rec.result);
+	}
+	iscandar_prefix_note(ISCANDAR_CENTER_PERCPU, size);
 	...
 }
--- a/lib/genalloc.c
+++ b/lib/genalloc.c
@@ -277,7 +277,25 @@
-unsigned long gen_pool_alloc_algo_owner(struct gen_pool *pool, size_t size, ...)
+unsigned long gen_pool_alloc_algo_owner(struct gen_pool *pool, size_t size, ...)
 {
+	if (iscandar_active() && iscandar_gen_pool_is_arena(pool)) {
+		struct IscandarBridgeRecord rec = { };
+
+		rec.op = ISCANDAR_OP_GENPOOL_ALLOC;
+		rec.size = size;
+		if (iscandar_bridge_call(&rec)
+		    || rec.status != ISCANDAR_BRIDGE_OK)
+			return 0;
+		return (unsigned long)
+			iscandar_offset_to_ptr(rec.result);
+	}
+	if (iscandar_active())
+		iscandar_prefix_note(ISCANDAR_CENTER_GENPOOL, size);
 	...
 }
@@ -487,5 +505,18 @@
-void gen_pool_free_owner(struct gen_pool *pool, unsigned long addr, size_t size)
+void gen_pool_free_owner(struct gen_pool *pool, unsigned long addr, size_t size)
 {
+	if (iscandar_gen_pool_is_arena(pool)
+	    && iscandar_ptr_in_arena((const void *)addr)) {
+		struct IscandarBridgeRecord rec = { };
+
+		rec.op = ISCANDAR_OP_GENPOOL_FREE;
+		rec.size = iscandar_ptr_to_offset((const void *)addr);
+		(void)iscandar_bridge_call(&rec);
+		return;
+	}
 	...
 }
